.TH "MEMCAPABLE" "1" "Mar 07, 2026" "1.1" "libmemcached-awesome"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
memcapable \- libmemcached Documentation
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
memcapable [options]
.sp
Check a memcached server\(aqs capabilities and compatibility.
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
\fBmemcapable\fP connects to the specified memcached server and tries to
determine its capabilities by running various commands and verifying the response.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-h hostname
Specify the hostname to connect to. The default is \fIlocalhost\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-p port
Specify the port number to connect to. The default is \fI11211\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-c
\fBabort(3) \%<https://\:linux\:.die\:.net/\:man/\:3/\:abort>\fP when detecting an error from the server.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-v
Print out the comparison when it detects an error from the server.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-t n
Set the timeout for an IO operation to/from the server to \fIn\fP seconds.
.UNINDENT
.SH "نکات (NOTES)"
.SS PROGRAM PREFIX
.sp
The prefix of this program is variable, i.e. it can be configured at build time.
.sp
Usually the client programs of \fBlibmemcached\-awesome\fP are prefixed with \fBmem\fP, like \fBmemcat\fP or \fBmemcp\fP\&.
.sp
It can be configured, though, to replace the prefix with something else like \fBmc\fP, in case of that,
the client programs of \fBlibmemcached\-awesome\fP would be called \fBmccat\fP, \fBmccp\fP, etc. respectively.
.SS CONTRIBUTED PROGRAM
.sp
This is a contributed program.
.sp
This program doesn\(aqt follow the standard flag/option scheme.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.sp
\fBmemcached(1) \%<https://\:linux\:.die\:.net/\:man/\:1/\:memcached>\fP
\fBlibmemcached(3) \%<https://\:linux\:.die\:.net/\:man/\:3/\:libmemcached>\fP
